; Start AmiGTA on MorphOS.
;
; RUN THIS FROM THE GAME'S OWN DRAWER:
;
;     cd Work:Games/AmiGTA
;     execute run
;
; There is nothing to assign. The game finds its data through PROGDIR:, the
; drawer the executable itself was loaded from, so it works wherever you put
; it - and PROGDIR: is set for a double-click from Ambient just as it is for a
; shell start.
;
; WHY THE REDIRECT IS NOT OPTIONAL. The engine reports everything it does on
; stdout: which screen mode it got, which blit method the screen turned out to
; support, the tile and map summaries, the frame timings, and the reason for
; every failure. Started from Ambient there is no console for any of that to go
; to, so the one thing you would need in order to say what went wrong is the
; one thing you would not have. It goes to a file beside the executable
; instead.
;
; NO `Stack` LINE, unlike the Amiga build's script. The MorphOS binary carries
; its own 1 MB stack in the __stack symbol (see native/morphos_gfx.c), so it
; gets it however it was started - from here, from a shell, or from an icon.
; The Amiga version cannot do that under libnix and needs the script.
gta-morphos >gta.log
